=====================================================================
KATHRYN CODE-PRODUCTIVITY CLASSIFICATION -- REPRODUCIBLE CRITERIA
=====================================================================

Purpose
-------
Every *real-code* line of a hardware design is classified into the 11 categories
below by a LANGUAGE-AGNOSTIC rule set that applies identically to
  (a) the Kathryn C++-embedded HDL   (src/example/o3/core), and
  (b) the reference RIDECORE Verilog (extSim/ridecore/src/fpga).

The scheme is a CROSS-PRODUCT of two independent axes:
  DOMAIN axis  = is the line about a CONTROL signal or a DATA signal?
                 Decided by looking the identifiers up in the KEYWORD LIST
                 below -- NOT by judgment. This is what makes it reproducible.
  KIND   axis  = what does the line DO: declare (HWD), compute (CL), move (DT),
                 connect (HC), or instantiate a module (MD)?

  {CTRL, DATA} x {HWD, CL, DT, HC}   +   MD, PARAM, HLH   =   11 categories

    CTRL_HWD  CTRL_CL  CTRL_DT  CTRL_HC      (control domain x 4 kinds)
    DATA_HWD  DATA_CL  DATA_DT  DATA_HC      (data    domain x 4 kinds)
    MD        PARAM    HLH                   (standalone, no domain)

There is NO priority / first-match-win (this is the key change from the old
8-category scheme). A line is tagged for EVERY category it qualifies for. When a
statement has more than one aspect, LINE-BREAK it so each physical line carries
exactly ONE clean category (score 1.0). Only a genuinely INSEPARABLE single token
(one port bundle carrying both a control and a data signal) is score-split 1/N.

Marker syntax (trailing comment, one per physical line):
    <code>            ///<CAT> <GROUP>              (single category, score 1)
    <code>            ///CTRL_HC+DATA_HC <GROUP>    (inseparable bundle: 1/2 each)
  where <CAT> is one of the 11 names above
  and   <GROUP> is a functional-block name (see GROUPS below).

A line carrying  ///DC  is EXCLUDED from the count (see EXCLUSIONS).


=====================================================================
THE DOMAIN AXIS -- ctrl vs data KEYWORD LIST (the authority)
=====================================================================
The DOMAIN of a line = the domain of the ELEMENT it writes / declares / connects
(its LHS/target for CL/DT/HWD; its port for HC). Look the identifier up here.
The list is by SEMANTIC ROLE; the names are examples (match the family, not the
exact spelling -- see the cross-core crosswalk at the end). '*' = prefix/suffix
wildcard.

CONTROL -- decides WHEN / WHETHER / WHICH:
  - clock / reset:        clk, reset
  - validity/occupancy/enable/write-enable:
        valid, busy, busyvec*, ready*, dstval*, we/we1/we2, wrrfen*, arfwe*,
        dpen*, issue*, issuevalid*, allocatable*, attachable, notfull*,
        notempty*, full/empty, hit*, finish, complete*, resolved*, clearbusy*,
        settagbusy*, renEn, isRenamable/isdispatable/is*Allocatable/isGenable,
        slotReady/entry_ready, sortReq/sortBit, com*Status/com*Cond/com*Avail,
        wbFin, rdUse/rsUse_*
  - stall/flush/kill/mispredict/recovery:
        stall_*, kill_*, kill_speculative*, prmiss, prsuccess, prcond*, inv*,
        invalid*, illegal*, holdMaster/holdSlave/killSlave/killIfTagMet,
        onMisPred/onSucPred, isBrMissPred/isBrSuccPred
  - speculation / recovery tags:
        spectag*/specTag, specbit*/spec, sptag*/spTag*Result, tagreg*, mask,
        mpft_valid*, brdepth, spectagfix, setspec*, isbranch*/isBranch,
        storebit/storeBit, branchvalid*/branchValid*, isAsRecvGrp
  - rename/producer tags + structural pointers  (DECISION 3):
        rrftag*/rrfIdx, prd/prs*, dst*_renamed, settag*, rem[], renRrfPtr,
        robid, comptr/comPtr*, finptr/finPtr, allocptr/allocPtr, freeptr,
        freenum, dispatchptr, retptr/retPtr, issueptr, checkIdx, reqPtr
  - handshake / pipeline sync / issue-request:
        req*, reqnum, grant/ack, dp1/dp2, exfin_*, stfin, sync*, SyncMeta/
        SyncPip, pip/zync/zyncc/autoSync/cwhile, onDispatch/onWriteBack/
        onCommit/onIssue, BroadCast/bc
  - branch-prediction control:
        bhr*, brcond*/brCond, brTaken, prediction, taken, *_PRIORITY consts

DATA -- the payload computed / moved:
  - pc / addresses:
        pc*, npc*, curPc/nextPc/fixPc/fixedPc/srcPc, praddr*/pred_addr, jmpaddr*,
        addr/dmem_addr/ldaddr/staddr/storeaddr/retaddr/mem_addr/memAddr/calAddr
  - operands / results / register-file data:
        src1/src2*, ex_src*, opr*/srcA/srcB/execSrc, arfdata/adat*/getArfData/
        archRegs, rrfdata/rdat*/com*data/datarr, wdata*/wrrfdata*/comdata/
        comData*, result*/exrslt*/res/out, val/data/rrfData/wbData/dpValue,
        dayta/daytas/stBufData/dmem_wdata/dmem_rdata/lddata*/stdata/storedata/
        retdata, phyIdx_* (payload-leaning; see note)
  - immediates:   imm*/imm1/imm2/imm_br/immGen/immBrGen   (the VALUE, not imm_type)
  - register indices  (DECISION 2):
        rd/rs1/rs2, rdIdx/rsIdx_*, dst/dstreg/dstarf*/comArcIdx
  - operation-SELECT fields  (DECISION 4):
        alu_op/aluOp, funct3/funct7/funct12, imm_type, src_a_sel/src_b_sel/
        rsSel_*, sel_lohi*, src*_signed/md_req_in_signed*, rs_ent/rsEnt,
        opcode/opc, md_req_op/md_req_out_sel, dmem_size/dmem_type, uses_rs*/wr_reg
  - instruction bits:   idata, inst*/instr, iMem*

The four firm decisions (kill the old ambiguity):
  1. NO first-match-win: tag every category a line qualifies for; line-break to
     separate, score-split only inseparable bundles.
  2. Register indices rd/rs1/rs2 (rdIdx/rsIdx_*) = DATA (operand-address payload
     at decode origin; a line that USES one as a table index is a separate CL/DT
     line whose domain follows ITS own target).
  3. Rename/producer tags + structural pointers = CONTROL (wakeup/bypass match,
     rename/commit bookkeeping -- never enter the ALU).
  4. Operation-select fields = DATA (decoded instruction fields; the immediate
     VALUE imm/imm_br is DATA too).

Note on phyIdx_* (the one genuine overload, srcOpr.h): tag the two assignment
sites individually -- phyIdx = phyEntry.data -> DATA; phyIdx = arfRen.rrfIdx.uext
-> CONTROL.

DOMAIN determination rule (reproducible):
  - A CL / DT / HWD line has exactly ONE target, so it is ALWAYS single-domain:
    CTRL and DATA never share such a line.
  - The domain follows the TARGET (the LHS being written / declared), NOT the RHS.
    For  a <<= b  (or  a = b ):  kind = DT (plain move) or CL (RHS computes);
    DOMAIN = domain of  a  (look  a  up in the list), regardless of  b . E.g.
    busy <<= b -> CTRL_DT ; pc <<= b -> DATA_DT ; comPtr <<= comPtr+1 -> CTRL_CL.
    (The RHS identifiers are counted on the lines that PRODUCE them.) If a target
    is not yet in the list, classify it by role and ADD it to the list.
  - Control-flow constructs with no data subject (clocked-process wrapper,
    if(reset)/stall/kill guards, FSM next-state, HDB flow blocks) are CONTROL by
    nature (kind = CL, so CTRL_CL).
  - HC domain = per-port. The ONLY line carrying both CTRL and DATA is a single
    inseparable HC bundle token -> split CTRL_HC + DATA_HC (0.5 each).
  - MD, PARAM, HLH have NO domain.


=====================================================================
THE KIND AXIS -- tag every kind that applies (do NOT pick one)
=====================================================================
Prefer to LINE-BREAK a statement so each physical line is one kind (score 1.0);
only score-share when a single token is inseparable.

MD  -- Module / struct declaration
    Concept: declaring or instantiating a MODULE or STRUCT (any composite user
    type), as opposed to a hardware PRIMITIVE (-> HWD). DOMAIN-LESS -> plain ///MD.
    Covers:
      - a struct/class/module TYPE header:  struct X{ ,  struct X: Module{ ,
        Verilog  module foo
      - a user-module / struct INSTANCE:  mMod(...) head ;  ModuleType inst
        (RegArch regArch, Rsvs rsvs, ...) ;  Verilog instance head
        reorderbuf rob / alu alice
    Distinct from HWD (a hardware primitive: reg/wire/mem/table/slot) and from HC
    (the struct members / wired args). NOTE: line-break the connectivity / members
    off the head -- see MODULE-DECL REFORMATTING.

HC  -- Hardware connectivity  (CTRL_HC / DATA_HC by port domain)
    Concept: an INTERFACE or CONNECTION -- signatures/parameter (port) lines,
    constructor-arg / instance connectivity, port-bundle structs + ref members,
    opr&-returning wrapper signatures, I/O tagging, instance port maps.
    Kathryn : (opr& op, opr& srcA, ...); struct RenameCmd{ opr& busy; ...};
              {tagMgmt.mpft} ctor-arg connectivity;  pm, regArch, storeBuf args;
              inline opr& alu <sig>; asInputGlob/asOutputGlob; ctor init-list binds.
    Verilog : input/output/inout port decls; instance port maps .op(alu_op).
    Domain: busy/valid/kill/sync port -> CTRL_HC ; data/pc/operand port -> DATA_HC.
    Inseparable bundle carrying both (PipStage& pm) -> CTRL_HC+DATA_HC (0.5 each).
    COMPUTED PORT ARG (Verilog): an instance port map whose arg is not a plain
    signal but an EXPRESSION -- logic/arith op (.enable(~stall_ID & ~stall_DP)),
    ternary mux (.wpc((sel)?a:b)), concat ({a,b}), or bit-slice (x[hi:lo]/x[b+:w])
    -- does TWO things on one line: connects the port (HC) AND computes the value
    (CL, per the concat/slice/ternary/logic-op = CL rule). Tag both, same domain as
    the port: X_HC+X_CL (0.5 each). This is symmetric with Kathryn, where such a
    compute is its own CL line (a zif guard / x = a & b) rather than hidden inside a
    port map. A plain .port(sig) stays pure HC. (Applied across RIDECORE: 138 lines.)
    LINE-BROKEN computed arg: when the expression spans multiple physical lines
    (a long concat .entvec({a[..], b[..],  /  c[..], d[..]})), EVERY physical line
    that itself carries a compute portion (a slice/concat token) is X_HC+X_CL, not
    just the first .name( line -- per the per-physical-line rule. (6 such
    continuation lines: oldest_finder.v, pipeline.v isunt_alu concats.)

HWD -- Hardware declaration  (CTRL_HWD / DATA_HWD by declared-element domain)
    Concept: declare a PERSISTENT hardware PRIMITIVE that holds data or named nets:
    data/control register, named wire/net, memory/table/slot storage, SlotMeta
    field layout. HWD is for ALL hardware types EXCEPT a module or struct -- a
    struct/class/module (type header OR instance) is MD, not HWD. Named constants
    -> PARAM.
    Kathryn : mReg/mWire/mExpr; WireSlot/RegSlot/Table/MemTable/mMem; SlotMeta.
    Verilog : reg/wire/logic; memory arrays reg[W:0] mem[0:N].
    Domain: reg busy -> CTRL_HWD ; reg [31:0] pc -> DATA_HWD.

CL  -- Combinational logic  (CTRL_CL / DATA_CL by target domain)
    Concept: COMPUTE a value via operators (arith/logic/compare/shift/bit-slice/
    concat/extension/mux/ternary; a datapath-select conditional). ALSO all
    control-flow / sequencing constructs: clocked-process wrapper
    always @(posedge ...), if(reset)/enable/stall/flush/kill guards, FSM
    next-state, HDB flow blocks (seq/par/zif/pip/loop/ztate/zcase), update-
    scheduling / priority -- these are CTRL_CL.
    Kathryn : out = srcA + srcB; shamt = srcB.sl(0,W); ~(fullBit >> shamt);
              ztate(op){zcase...}; g(...) concat; .uext/.sext; pip/zync/cwhile;
              SET_ASM_PRI_TO_MANUAL/AUTO.
    Verilog : assign y=a+b; case(op)...; sel?a:b; {31'b0,in1==in2};
              always @(posedge clk); if(reset); assign stall/kill/valid.
    Domain: assign kill=... -> CTRL_CL ; assign y=a+b -> DATA_CL.

DT  -- Data transfer  (CTRL_DT / DATA_DT by target domain)
    Concept: MOVE / COPY / ROUTE / STORE a value with NO operators -- plain
    signal RHS, struct field, indexed read; register write of a signal; array/
    table/struct element write; RESET-VALUE write.
    Kathryn : busyTemp = busySlot; busySlot <<= busyTemp; _table[idx] <<= dpValue;
              makeResetEvent/makeColResetEvent/makeDefEvent (reset-value reg.).
    Verilog : assign y=x; q<=d; data[finptr]<=stdata; reset-branch q<=0.
    Domain: busy<=issue / busy<=0 -> CTRL_DT ; pc<=npc / pc<=0 -> DATA_DT.
    Boundary vs CL: table/array/struct INDEXING is access -> DT; bit-SLICE /
    concat / extend is compute -> CL.

PARAM -- Parameter / constant  (domain-less)
    Concept: a NAMED CONSTANT / PARAMETER definition -- sizes, counts, encodings,
    constant values. Explicitly-constant forms only.
    Kathryn : mVal/mPmVal; static/const/constexpr numeric consts (incl *_PRIORITY);
              O3_PARAM_STR(name) field/opcode/width identifiers.
    Verilog : parameter; localparam; `define value macros (`REG_SEL, widths, ops).
    A plain MUTABLE host var (int idx=-1, reassigned later) stays HLH.

HLH -- Host-language helper  (domain-less)
    Concept: host-language CONTROL-STRUCTURE scaffolding -- neither hardware nor a
    constant; the glue the host language needs to elaborate the hardware.
    Kathryn : for/while host loops; std:: containers; templates; structured
              bindings auto[a,b]=...; glue lambdas; function-like macros
              (#define str(name)); plain mutable int/bool.
    Verilog : genvar; generate/for; integer i; initialization loops.


=====================================================================
MODULE-DECL REFORMATTING (line-break MD off HC)
=====================================================================
Because MD (the module head) and HC (its wired connectivity) are two kinds, and
there is no first-match-win, line-break every module-instance declaration so each
is its own physical line. Layout-only edit -- valid C++/Verilog, no semantics:

  // before
  RegArch  regArch {tagMgmt.mpft};
  mMod(prob, Rob, pm, regArch, storeBuf);
  // after
  RegArch  regArch            ///MD  <GROUP>
  {tagMgmt.mpft};             ///HC  <GROUP>   (per-arg domain; tagMgmt/mpft=CTRL_HC)
  mMod(prob, Rob,             ///MD  <GROUP>
    pm, regArch, storeBuf);   ///HC  <GROUP>


=====================================================================
KRIDE WORKED CONVENTIONS  (locked from the gold exemplars arf.h + core.h)
=====================================================================
These resolve the recurring Kride calls so the two exemplars reproduce exactly:
  - rename table / renRrfPtr / rrfIdx / rename* = CONTROL (decision 3). So the
    ARF is mostly control bookkeeping (busy + rename); only archRegs / *data /
    comData are DATA.
  - arch-register indices renArcIdx / comArcIdx / archIdx = DATA (decision 2);
    the index only STEERS, but the identifier itself is DATA payload.
  - SET_ASM_PRI_TO_MANUAL / _AUTO = CTRL_CL (update-scheduling control). A zif /
    guard = CTRL_CL when it gates a control action; a datapath zif that SELECTS a
    value = CL by the selected value's domain.
  - a struct/class/module header OR instance = MD (RenameCmd, PreRenGrp,
    PreRenGrp preRenGrp[]); Table / RegSlot / WireSlot / mReg / mWire / mExpr =
    HWD (domain by target: busy/rename -> CTRL_HWD, archRegs -> DATA_HWD).
  - a SlotMeta header (inline SlotMeta smX{...}) = HWD, domain by its FIELDS:
    all-control -> CTRL_HWD (smRsvO/I, smMPFT, smARFBusy/Renamed), all-data ->
    DATA_HWD (smRsvBranch/Alu/Mul, smARFData), MIXED control+data fields ->
    CTRL_HWD+DATA_HWD bundle (smFetch, smDecBase, smDecShard, smRsvBase,
    smStoreBuf, smLdSt, smRRF, smROB). NO majority-collapse: any slot storing
    both a control field (busy/valid/spec/rdUse/isBranch/*ptr...) AND a data
    field (pc/inst/imm/operand/rd*Idx...) is a bundle. Its field-name and width
    list lines = PARAM.
  - method / ctor SIGNATURE = HC, domain by its params (per-line for multi-line
    signatures). A ctor with a hardware param (Arf(Mpft&)) = CTRL_HC; a ctor /
    method with only a host param (Core(int x), flow()) = HLH. A port-bundle
    param that carries both control and data (RenameCmd: renEn/specTag control +
    renArcIdx data ; PipStage& pm) = CTRL_HC+DATA_HC (0.5 each). A method-call
    line wiring several args splits like any connectivity line (per-arg domain,
    consecutive-arg grouping, no reorder).
  - reset-value registration makeResetEvent / makeColResetEvent / makeDefEvent =
    DT, domain by the register written (busy.makeResetEvent -> CTRL_DT).
  - host scaffolding: for/while host loops, `int idx = -1;`, C++ `if(override)`
    on a host bool = HLH. A host lambda / structured-binding / std::pair typedef
    used as elaboration glue = HLH.
  - MODULE / whole-object domain table (wired arg, member ref, ctor param, bind):
      CTRL_HC  : bc/BroadCast, mpft, tagMgmt, taggen
      bundle   : pm/pm.ldSt, rsv/rsvs/RsvBase, rob/Rob, pDisp, regArch/RegArch,
                 storeBuf/StoreBuf, lss/LdStStage, bp/ByPass -> CTRL_HC+DATA_HC
                 (each carries both a control routing/rename/tag part AND a data
                 part -- e.g. ByPass = {rrfIdx tag(CTRL), val(DATA)}; RegArch =
                 rename/busy(CTRL) + register data(DATA)).
  - WHOLE-SLOT rule: a whole Slot/RegSlot/WireSlot reference (declaration, bind
    `RegSlot& x = ...`, whole move `x <<= y`, .makeResetEvent(), or a
    `RegSlot&/WireSlot& x` param) takes the domain of its SlotMeta -- pure-data
    meta -> DATA (smRsvAlu/ARFData...), pure-control meta -> CTRL (smRsvO/I,
    smMPFT, smARFBusy...), MIXED meta -> CTRL+DATA bundle (smFetch/raw,
    smDecBase/dcd,dcw, smDecShard/dcdShared, smRsvBase/execSrc,src,iw,des,
    smLdSt/lsRes, smROB/com*Entry,selectedEntry, smStoreBuf/retireSlot). NO
    predominant-role collapse. A specific sub-FIELD access src(rrftag)/src(rdUse)/
    src(spec) uses ITS OWN domain (that's how the control fields still get counted
    as control).
    A method CALL through a module uses its ARGS' domains, NOT the module's
    (regArch.rrf.onWback(rrftag, data) = CTRL_HC+DATA_HC by the args; a no-arg
    whole-object call like stBuf.flow() takes the object's domain = bundle).
  - RETURN rule: `return <plain signal>` or `return {a,b}` (braced plain refs) =
    HC (domain by the returned value / bundle); `return <expr with operators or a
    mux/select>` = CL (domain by the value). A multi-element braced return whose
    elements are a control+data pair = CTRL_HC+DATA_HC.
  - a function/lambda CALL that returns a computed value assigned to a wire
    (srcA = getAluSrcA(src); isKilled = bc.checkIsKill(...)) = CL by target
    domain. A connectivity call that wires args into another block
    (rob.onWriteBack(src(rrftag)); bp.addSrc(tag,data)) = HC, per-arg domain.
  - the flow() method signature = HLH (host method, no hw param).
  - CYCLE-ADVANCING HDB headers (pip/pipe/zync/zyncc/cwhile/while/loop/wait/seq/
    state) = CTRL_HWD+CTRL_CL (0.5 each): they BOTH instantiate control-state
    hardware (the flow-block state/sync/counter register -- SR_ST# in generated
    Verilog) AND implement control sequencing logic. This keeps the comparison
    SYMMETRIC with RIDECORE, where the same FSM is two separate lines: reg state
    (CTRL_HWD) + always@(posedge) case(state) (CTRL_CL). A single Kathryn header
    replaces both, so it earns both credits.
  - COMBINATIONAL HDB headers (zif/zelif/zelse, zcase/ztate-as-decode, par, pick)
    create NO state register = pure CL: a zif gating a control action = CTRL_CL;
    a datapath zif/ztate SELECTING a value = CL by the selected value's domain.


=====================================================================
EXCLUSIONS -- never marked (not real code, or explicitly excluded)
=====================================================================
  - Comment / documentation lines: pure //, ///, /////-only lines and multi-line
    /** ... */ doc blocks. (A real code line that merely ENDS with a trailing
    // note still gets its category.)
  - Lines carrying ///DC = the universal EXCLUDE marker (kept for audit trail):
      * Kathryn : simulation instrumentation (initProbe, tryInitProbe,
                  dataStructProbGrp.*.init(...)).
      * Verilog : (a) dual-issue path DUPLICATION (the 2nd instruction's copy of a
                  datapath / instance, e.g. src_manager srcmng2) -- the bulk; and
                  (b) DISABLED-FEATURE logic Kathryn also omits: the gshare branch
                  predictor's bhr/prcond STORAGE + plumbing (rs_branch.v; predictor
                  ports are commented out in pipeline.v and prcond is hardwired 0),
                  mirroring Kathryn's disabled smBtb/gshare = DC. Excluded so both
                  sides count UNIQUE, LIVE logic once. NUANCE: only the disabled
                  STORAGE/plumbing is DC -- control scaffolding that still functions
                  under static not-taken prediction (branchvalid/inv/praddr in
                  pipeline.v) stays COUNTED.
  - Soft-deleted files: a WHOLLY-DEAD source file (every module uninstantiated,
    e.g. the latched ram_sync.v -- module ram_sync_2r2w, never used; the design
    uses the nolatch BRAM variant) is MOVED to a fpga/deleted/ folder rather than
    ///DC-tagged line-by-line. countMeasure.py SKIP_DIRS includes "deleted" so the
    whole folder is pruned from the walk. (Distinct from ///DC, which excludes
    individual lines inside a live file.)
  - Preprocessor / structural noise: #include / `include; namespace X {;
    #ifndef/#define GUARD/#endif include-guards; `timescale; blank lines;
    lone braces/keywords ( {  }  };  begin  end  endmodule  endcase  endgenerate ).
    (`define constant lines are NOT noise -- they are PARAM; only `include/directive
    lines are excluded.)
  - Host assert(...) / debug.


=====================================================================
MARKING CONVENTION
=====================================================================
  - Trailing ///<CAT> <GROUP> on each real-code line, whitespace-aligned.
  - EVERY real-code physical line is tagged; a statement spanning N lines counts
    N times. Continuation lines (wrapped expressions, call args, return values,
    SlotMeta field/width lists) INHERIT the statement's category = the nearest
    ///<CAT> tag above them (script: tagContinuation.py). A multi-line instance =>
    MD head line + HC on each wired-arg / .port(x) line (unless the whole instance
    is ///DC -> all excluded). Only bare closers ( ) } ; , ), structural keywords
    (begin/end/endmodule/endcase), bare else-junctions (}else{ / }zelse{ /
    end else begin), host assert(...), comments, and blank lines stay untagged.
  - <GROUP> reuses the aligned block names below; the CATEGORY axis is primary,
    the GROUP is the secondary breakdown. Keep Kathryn and RIDECORE group names
    ALIGNED so per-block comparison is meaningful.
  - Preserve existing correct markers; fix malformed ones.


=====================================================================
COUNTING
=====================================================================
  Category regex : ///\s*(<ALT>(?:\+(?:<ALT>))*)\s+(\w+)
      where <ALT> = alternation of the 11 category names (longest-first).
      The whole category expression (with any '+' parts) is capture group 1;
      the group name is group 2. Split group 1 on '+'; a K-way packed tag credits
      1/K score to EACH category -- e.g. ///CTRL_HC+DATA_HC -> +0.5 each. A
      single-category tag scores 1.0.
  Exclude regex  : ///\s*DC            (skip any line that matches this)
  Aggregate per-category and per-(category x group); category totals may be
  FRACTIONAL. countMeasure.py [DIR] reports one side; countCompare.py reports
  Kathryn (./core) vs RIDECORE (../../../extSim/ridecore/src/fpga) with the
  derived rollups CTRL total (= sum CTRL_*) and DATA total (= sum DATA_*) and the
  per-category reduction %. countMeasure.py also WARNS on any stray uppercase
  ///tag that is not a valid category (catches leftover old tags).


