GROUPS  (functional blocks; keep aligned across both sides)
=====================================================================
CORE   FETCH   DECODE   DISPATCH
RSV_SHARED   RSV_ALU   RSV_BRANCH   RSV_LDST   RSV_MUL
EXEC_ALU   EXEC_BRANCH   EXEC_LDST   EXEC_MUL
ROB   COMMIT   ARF   RRF   MPFT   TAG   STOREBUF   SHARED_COMP

pipeline.v decomposition (RIDECORE pools many blocks into one 1935-line file;
assign each region a GROUP):
  PRIMARY  -- nearest instantiated submodule wins:
    pipeline_if pipe_if -> FETCH ; tag_generator taggen -> TAG ;
    decoder dec1/dec2 -> DECODE ; arf aregfile -> ARF ;
    rrf rregfile + rrf_freelistmanager rrf_fl -> RRF ;
    sourceoperand_manager / src_manager / imm_gen / brimm_gen /
      rs_requestgenerator -> DISPATCH ;
    rs_alu / rs_ldst / rs_branch / rs_mul + alloc_issue_ino -> RSV_* ;
    exunit_alu byakko/suzaku / exunit_ldst seiryu / exunit_branch kirin / dmem
      -> EXEC_* ;  miss_prediction_fix_table mpft -> MPFT ;
    reorderbuf rob -> ROB / COMMIT .
  SECONDARY -- signal-suffix prefix clusters for free-standing assign/always
    lines between instances:
    *_id -> DECODE ; pc*/npc*/inst*/*_if -> FETCH ; sptag*/spec*/tagreg*/brdepth
    -> TAG ; mpft_* -> MPFT ; adat*/abusy*/*tag/settag* -> ARF ; rdat*/rvalid*/
    com*data/*_renamed/rrfptr/freenum -> RRF ; comptr*/comnum/arfwe*/dp*_addr/
    exfin_*/stcommit -> ROB/COMMIT ; *_alu1/_alu2/_ldst/_branch/_mul incl buf_*
    -> RSV_*/EXEC_* ; sb_*/st*/hitsb/ldaddr/retptr -> STOREBUF .
  TIE-BREAK -- inside a .port(sig) map, the instance's group wins over the wire's
    prefix group.


=====================================================================
RIDECORE (Verilog) WORKED CONVENTIONS
=====================================================================
  - PRESERVE every existing ///DC line EXACTLY (never re-tag, never count) --
    it excludes RIDECORE's dual-issue path DUPLICATION so both sides count UNIQUE
    logic once (Kathryn covers both instructions with one loop/aggregator body).
  - module <name> header = MD ; a module INSTANCE head (alu alice / src_a_mux samx
    / reorderbuf rob) = MD ; its .port(sig) map lines = HC per-port domain.
  - input/output/inout port decls = HC, domain by the port (crosswalk below):
      CTRL_HC: clk, reset, *_we/we, dstval, issue, prmiss/prsuccess, valid/busy,
               spectag/specbit/spectagfix/tagreg*, kill_speculative, brcond,
               stall_*/kill_*, *ptr, finish, ready, alloc*
      DATA_HC: ex_src*/rs1/rs2/src*, pc/praddr/npc/jmpaddr*/addr, imm, result/out,
               *data, inst/idata, rd/rs*(indices), alu_op/src_a/src_b/opcode/
               funct*/imm_type/*_sel/*_signed (op-select = DATA, decision 4)
  - reg / wire DECLARATION (no assign) = HWD, domain by the signal (reg busy ->
    CTRL_HWD ; wire [DATA_LEN] alusrc -> DATA_HWD). `wire x = <expr>;` (decl +
    continuous assign) = CL by x's domain (the assign dominates).
  - always @(posedge/negedge clk) wrapper + if(reset)/enable guards = CTRL_CL
    (clocked sequencing). always @(*) combinational block = CL by the target it
    computes. case(...) / a ? b : c = CL by target.
  - assign y = x; (plain copy) = DT ; q <= d; (plain reg write, incl reset q<=0)
    = DT -- domain by the target y/q. assign y = <operators> = CL by target.
  - `include / `default_nettype / `timescale / endmodule / endcase / begin / end
    / lone ) ; = structural, UNTAGGED.


